AIM:
Write a Program to implement control flow statements and looping statements in python.

ALGORITHM:
ALGORITHM: BEST ALL-ROUND PERFORMER

1. Start.

2. Store the batting, bowling and fielding statistics
   of four cricket players.

3. Calculate the Strike Rate of each player:
      Strike Rate = (Runs / Balls Faced) × 100

4. Calculate the Economy Rate of each player:
      Economy Rate = Runs Conceded / Overs Bowled

5. For each player, determine batting performance:
      a. If Runs >= 50 AND Strike Rate >= 120,
         display "Excellent Batter".
      b. Else if Runs >= 30 AND Strike Rate >= 100,
         display "Good Batter".
      c. Else if Runs >= 20,
         display "Average Batter".
      d. Else display "Poor Batter".

6. Determine bowling performance:
      a. If Wickets >= 3 AND Economy Rate <= 6,
         display "Excellent Bowler".
      b. Else if Wickets >= 2 AND Economy Rate <= 8,
         display "Good Bowler".
      c. Else if Wickets >= 1,
         display "Average Bowler".
      d. Else display "Poor Bowler".

7. Determine fielding performance:
      a. If Catches >= 2,
         display "Outstanding Fielder".
      b. Else if Catches == 1,
         display "Active Fielder".
      c. Else display "Needs Improvement".

8. Determine overall All-Rounder performance:
      a. If Batter is Excellent AND Bowler is Excellent,
         display "Star All-Rounder".
      b. Else if Batter is Good AND Bowler is Good,
         display "Strong All-Rounder".
      c. Else if either Batter or Bowler is Good,
         display "Supporting All-Rounder".
      d. Else display "Needs Improvement".

9. Display all calculated results.

10. Stop.
